From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150: route SPMI periph_irq through PDC

The SM8150 SPMI PMIC arbiter still describes its periph_irq as a raw GIC
SPI, unlike SM8250 and newer Qualcomm SoCs which route the same pin
through the PDC. A raw GIC parent has no useful set-wake path, so a PMIC
GPIO child's enable_irq_wake() cannot arm the Qualcomm PDC. This blocks
the standard extcon-usb-gpio VBUS wake path.

Move the parent to PDC pin 1, which qcom,pdc-ranges maps to GIC SPI 481.
This is SoC integration, not board policy; the board overlay should only
describe the PM8150 GPIO10 VBUS input and its pinctrl.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@localhost>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
index 2f944a361..1828462bf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
@@ -4552,7 +4553,7 @@ spmi_bus: spmi@c440000 {
 			      <0x0 0x0c40a000 0x0 0x0026000>;
 			reg-names = "core", "chnls", "obsrvr", "intr", "cnfg";
 			interrupt-names = "periph_irq";
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 481 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupts-extended = <&pdc 1 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			qcom,ee = <0>;
 			qcom,channel = <0>;
 			#address-cells = <2>;
